      "writtenOn": "2024-10-17T07:52:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The HVC call itself is presumably non-preemptible, so we\u0027re talking about different types of \u0027blocking\u0027 here. To re-phrase Todd\u0027s question, does your hook handler need to schedule (e.g. does it take a mutex, or a preemptible lock, or something like so?)? If not, then the restricted hooks are not needed -- spending time non-preemptible at EL2 is totally compatible with the standard vendor hooks.",
      "parentUuid": "2774351d_1b5c482f",
      "revId": "4ff3547c9d2c13c8637d10d8116157f7135311d6",
